{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "03593",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 1.2,
      "end_seconds": 6.53,
      "duration_seconds": 5.33,
      "text": "Afternoon, doctor. They're in and comfortable, and I have the measurements ready."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 9.52,
      "end_seconds": 14.62,
      "duration_seconds": 5.1,
      "text": "Thanks. Hello, come in, sit down. What brings you in today?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 15.46,
      "end_seconds": 19.06,
      "duration_seconds": 3.6,
      "text": "I wanted to get constipation looked at."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 20.81,
      "end_seconds": 22.76,
      "duration_seconds": 1.95,
      "text": "Did it come on recently?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 24.79,
      "end_seconds": 28.49,
      "duration_seconds": 3.7,
      "text": "it's been three weeks, I'm fairly sure"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 30.06,
      "end_seconds": 32.92,
      "duration_seconds": 2.86,
      "text": "would you say mild, moderate or severe?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 37.98,
      "end_seconds": 39.44,
      "duration_seconds": 1.46,
      "text": "Mild, I'd say."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 40.81,
      "end_seconds": 42.82,
      "duration_seconds": 2.01,
      "text": "any other symptoms with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 43.51,
      "end_seconds": 56.02,
      "duration_seconds": 12.51,
      "text": "When it starts I tend to get dry skin and hair as well. I've been feeling flat and slowed down too, for about four days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 57.82,
      "end_seconds": 62.3,
      "duration_seconds": 4.48,
      "text": "Have you had constipation before, or is this the first time?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 63.28,
      "end_seconds": 71.7,
      "duration_seconds": 8.42,
      "text": "yes, something like this happened a couple of years ago, and it went away on its own"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 72.54,
      "end_seconds": 79.41,
      "duration_seconds": 6.87,
      "text": "Doctor, I've got the readings for you. Oxygen saturation is 97 percent, pulse 73, pressure 121 over 75."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 80.24,
      "end_seconds": 81.15,
      "duration_seconds": 0.91,
      "text": "Alright, thanks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 82.64,
      "end_seconds": 86.73,
      "duration_seconds": 4.09,
      "text": "now I'm going to do a a short physical check"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 88.22,
      "end_seconds": 91.24,
      "duration_seconds": 3.02,
      "text": "Okay, I'll listen to your chest now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 100.36,
      "end_seconds": 104.71,
      "duration_seconds": 4.35,
      "text": "your pulse is slow and and your reflexes relax slowly"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 108.21,
      "end_seconds": 111.09,
      "duration_seconds": 2.88,
      "text": "thank you, you can get dressed"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 128.85,
      "end_seconds": 131.48,
      "duration_seconds": 2.63,
      "text": "Have you had any weight loss?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 132.23,
      "end_seconds": 134.38,
      "duration_seconds": 2.15,
      "text": "definitely no weight loss"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 135.79,
      "end_seconds": 142.03,
      "duration_seconds": 6.24,
      "text": "alright, have you had any palpitations, hearing voices or thoughts of harming myself?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 143.78,
      "end_seconds": 151.19,
      "duration_seconds": 7.41,
      "text": "no palpitations, hearing voices or thoughts of harming myself, none of it it"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 151.73,
      "end_seconds": 155.02,
      "duration_seconds": 3.29,
      "text": "Mm, okay. Anything different when you pass water?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 156.27,
      "end_seconds": 159.91,
      "duration_seconds": 3.64,
      "text": "that's normal as far as I know"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 165.38,
      "end_seconds": 166.77,
      "duration_seconds": 1.39,
      "text": "Neurologically, anything strange?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 168.36,
      "end_seconds": 170.18,
      "duration_seconds": 1.82,
      "text": "no weakness or anything"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 171.09,
      "end_seconds": 174.36,
      "duration_seconds": 3.27,
      "text": "Has anyone ever diagnosed you with something?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 175.43,
      "end_seconds": 179.58,
      "duration_seconds": 4.15,
      "text": "I've had diabetes for nearly five years now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 181.17,
      "end_seconds": 184.37,
      "duration_seconds": 3.2,
      "text": "Mm, okay. Any surgery in the past?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 185.14,
      "end_seconds": 188.96,
      "duration_seconds": 3.82,
      "text": "just my tonsils removed, as a teenager"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 189.89,
      "end_seconds": 193.41,
      "duration_seconds": 3.52,
      "text": "Is there anything relevant on the family side?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 194.77,
      "end_seconds": 198.85,
      "duration_seconds": 4.08,
      "text": "hmm, my grandfather had a a stroke"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 200.57,
      "end_seconds": 203.47,
      "duration_seconds": 2.9,
      "text": "now some background about your lifestyle"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 205.28,
      "end_seconds": 221.09,
      "duration_seconds": 15.81,
      "text": "Nothing, I'm teetotal. I gave up cigarettes last spring. I hardly move around during the day. I'm a plumber, lots of bending and kneeling. My partner and our baby."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 221.89,
      "end_seconds": 225.4,
      "duration_seconds": 3.51,
      "text": "Let me ask about allergies, anything at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 226.84,
      "end_seconds": 229.3,
      "duration_seconds": 2.46,
      "text": "Yes, diclofenac. I get wheezing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 239.7,
      "end_seconds": 242.86,
      "duration_seconds": 3.16,
      "text": "Is there any regular medication you use?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 243.59,
      "end_seconds": 246.27,
      "duration_seconds": 2.68,
      "text": "no, nothing at the moment"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 264.8,
      "end_seconds": 292.19,
      "duration_seconds": 27.39,
      "text": "We should do a thyroid test for slowing and cold intolerance. We should do a blood count for tiredness. We'll check the thyroid before deciding on any antidepressant. If the symptoms get worse, that's the point to come in urgently. I'd like to see you again after the results. What are the next steps as you understand them?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 296.67,
      "end_seconds": 302.31,
      "duration_seconds": 5.64,
      "text": "So, I come back after the results. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 303.75,
      "end_seconds": 307.45,
      "duration_seconds": 3.7,
      "text": "Yes, exactly right. Does all of that make sense?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 309.23,
      "end_seconds": 312.31,
      "duration_seconds": 3.08,
      "text": "Um, alright, thanks, take care."
    }
  ]
}